                    "text": "param dry_wet_mix 0.5 @min 0 @max 1",
                    "varname": "dry_wet_mix"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-37",
                    "linecount": 64,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 578.0, 942.0 ],
                    "text": "================================================================================\nchorus_bbd_blep_clock_matrix — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nOVERVIEW\nA standalone stereo BBD Chorus/Flanger Matrix combining Leonardo Gabrielli, Stefano D'Angelo, and Stefano Squartini's \"Antialiasing in BBD Chips Using BLEP\" (DAFx-25 Paper 29, Sections 2.1, 3 & 4.3, Algorithm 1, Eq. 1–2) with Jaromír Mačák's Electro-Harmonix Deluxe Electric Mistress nonlinear RC astable clock generator (DAFx-16 Paper 59, Sections 2.1–2.2, Eq. 8–11). Instead of approximating a BBD with a smooth digital delay line, this effect clocks a true 256-bucket discrete-time shift register at F_CLK(t). When F_CLK is lowered into the audio range (4–15 kHz), it produces authentic BBD-Generated Aliasing (BGA: musical foldback sidebands at k*F_CLK +/- f0), while a continuous-time PolyBLEP step residual eliminates harsh digital Simulation-Generated Aliasing (SGA) at every sample-and-hold transition!\n\nINLETS & OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: Stereo Audio Input (Tuba; mono in1 auto-normalizes to stereo)\n- in3: Optional Envelope Modulator [0..1] (shifts the astable comparator threshold U_THD on loud attacks)\n- in4: Optional 1-Bar Audio-Rate Phasor [0..1] (syncs LFO to host tempo when patched)\n- out1 / out2: Stereo PolyBLEP Clock-Stepped BBD Chorus Output\n\nPARAMETERS (7)\n\n1. lfo_rate_hz\n   - Range: 0.08 to 5.00 Hz (LFO Sweep Rate, Default: 0.45 Hz)\n   - Taper: Direct frequency in Hz.\n   - Function: Controls the speed of the triangle integrator/comparator LFO (DAFx-16 Eq. 4).\n\n2. sweep_depth\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (Clock Excursion Depth, Default: 0.55)\n   - Taper: Linear modulation depth.\n   - Function: Controls how wide the BBD clock frequency swings around bbd_clock_khz. At 0.0, engages the static \"Filter Matrix\" metallic comb resonator mode (DAFx-16 Section 3).\n\n3. bbd_clock_khz\n   - Range: 4.0 to 48.0 kHz (Nominal BBD Clock Frequency F_CLK, Default: 18.0 kHz -> ~14.2 ms chorus delay across 256 buckets)\n   - Taper: Direct clock frequency in kHz.\n   - Function: High clocks (25–48 kHz, 5–10 ms delay) yield pristine, silvery stereo chorusing/flanging; lower clocks (4–12 kHz, 21–64 ms delay) intentionally expose gritty, musical BBD clock-foldback aliasing (BGA) while PolyBLEP keeps the digital simulation clean!\n\n4. astable_curve\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (Nonlinear RC Astable Charging Law, Default: 0.55)\n   - Taper: Linear blend between symmetric sweep (0.0) and Mačák's logarithmic capacitor charging law T_clock = -2*tau*ln((U_Max - U_THD)/U_Max) (1.0, DAFx-16 Eq. 9).\n   - Function: Imparts the unmistakable \"lingering at the top, swooping at the bottom\" sweep trajectory of vintage EHX BBD modulation pedals.\n\n5. matrix_feedback\n   - Range: -0.85 to +0.85 (BBD Regeneration / Color Feedback, Default: +0.30)\n   - Taper: Linear bipolar feedback with internal tanh saturation guard.\n   - Function: Emphasizes the BBD comb resonances for hollow Deluxe Electric Mistress / metallic dubstep chorus textures.\n\n6. recon_filter_hz\n   - Range: 1500.0 to 18000.0 Hz (Post-BBD Anti-Imaging Reconstruction Lowpass Cutoff, Default: 7500.0 Hz)\n   - Taper: Direct frequency in Hz.\n   - Function: Controls how much of the BBD clock-foldback sparkle (BGA) passes into the stereo output.\n\n7. dry_wet_mix\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0% Dry to 100% Wet; Default: 0.50 = 50/50 Chorus)\n   - Taper: Constant-power cosine/sine crossfade.\n   - Function: Balances the dry tuba against the PolyBLEP BBD chorus.\n",
                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                }
            }
        ],
